1

               U. S. Department of Commerce, U. S. Census Bureau

              X-13ARIMA-SEATS monthly seasonal adjustment Method,
                          Release Version 1.1 Build 61


           This software application provides an enhanced version of
             Statistics Canada's X-11-ARIMA extension (Dagum, 1980)
                 of the X-11 variant of the Census Method II of
                      Shiskin, Young and Musgrave (1967).

            It also provides an ARIMA model-based method following
       Hillmer and Tiao (1982) and Burman (1980) that is very similar
       to the update of the method of SEATS (Gomez and Maravall, 1996)
                produced at the Bank of Spain by G. Caporello and
               A. Maravall for TSW (Caporello and Maravall, 2004).
          The present application includes additional enhancements.

         X-13ARIMA-SEATS includes an automatic ARIMA model selection procedure
          based largely on the procedure of Gomez and Maravall (1998)
            as implemented in TRAMO (1996) and subsequent revisions.

              Primary Programmers: Brian Monsell, Mark Otto and,
                 for the ARIMA model-based signal extraction,
                      Gianluca Caporello and Victor Gomez


     Series Title- PAYEMS with span + modelspan subsetting
     Series Name- span-modelspan
     Jul 18, 2026  15.00.09 

        -Period covered-  1st month,2005 to  8th month,2025
        -Type of run - multiplicative seasonal adjustment

        -Sigma limits for graduating extreme values are  1.5 and  2.5 .
        -3x3 moving average used in section 1 of each iteration, 
         3x5 moving average in section 2 of iterations B and C,
         moving average for final seasonal factors chosen by Global MSR.
        -Spectral plots generated for selected series
        -Spectral plots generated for series starting in 2017.Sep
  span-modelspan.out  program output file
  span-modelspan.err  program error file
  span-modelspan.udg  seasonal adjustment and model diagnostics file
        PAYEMS with span + modelspan subsetting            PAGE   1, SERIES span-modelspan

     Contents of spc file span-modelspan.spc

 Line #
 ------
      1: # EDGE CASE: span and modelspan subsetting.
      2: #   span      = restricts the range of the series that is analysed / adjusted.
      3: #   modelspan = restricts the (narrower) range used to estimate the regARIMA
      4: #               model, while the full span is still adjusted.
      5: # The full data file is 2000.01-2025.08 (308 obs); this run analyses 2005.01
      6: # onward and estimates the model only through 2020.12.
      7: series{
      8:   title     = "PAYEMS with span + modelspan subsetting"
      9:   file      = "payems.dat"
     10:   start     = 2000.01
     11:   period    = 12
     12:   span      = (2005.01, )
     13:   modelspan = (, 2020.12)
     14: }
     15: transform{
     16:   function = log
     17: }
     18: automdl{ }
     19: forecast{
     20:   maxlead = 24
     21: }
     22: x11{ }
